Pacman
------

This is a clone of the original Pac-Man from Namco, as I remember , and I played 
for the first time on an Atari 130 XL in the early 90s.
But Paul Neaves Pac-Man clone has inspired me greatly.
One of the main goals of this implementation is a SDL Application with very
less use of CPU power.


Install hint
------------

You need make, g++, pkg-config and the development packages of SDL2,
SDL2_image, SDL2_ttf and SDL2_mixer. Run "make" in the pacman directory,
then start the game with "./pacman". See README.md for installation.


